        rules: {
          objective: 'Advance through all levels (2 to Ace) and win a hand at Level Ace with the correct finishing order (1st & 2nd, or 1st & 3rd).',
          gameplay: 'Deal all 108 cards, 27 to each player. The starting player leads any legal combination; other players may pass or play a higher combination of the same type, while bombs and special high combinations can overcall. When three players pass, the last player to play wins control and leads next. A hand ends as players empty their hands, and the finishing order determines team level advancement.',
          keyRules: [
            'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Guan Dan (??).',
            'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: Scoring summary: Scoring follows the game-specific point or pot rules.',
            'Winning condition: Advance through all levels (2 to Ace) and win a hand at Level Ace with the correct finishing order (1st & 2nd, or 1st & 3rd).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Coordinate with your partner. If your partner is close to finishing, help them by winning tricks and leading cards they can beat.',
          intermediate: 'The Wild Card Advantage: at each level, the hearts of that level are wild. For example, at Level 7, the 7 of hearts is wild. Use it to complete straights or bombs.',
          advanced: 'Bomb Timing: Bombs are powerful but limited. Save them for critical moments, such as when your partner is about to finish or to stop opponents from finishing 1st & 2nd.',
          tips: [
            "Count the level cards. If you're at Level 5, track all four 5s (especially the 5 of hearts wild card).",
            'Finishing 1st & 2nd gives a massive +4 level boost. Prioritize this if possible.',
            "If you're losing, try to finish 2nd to prevent opponents from getting the +4 boost.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
